    {"question": "What is virus?", "ground_truth": "Virus is a microscopic infectious agent that requires host cells to replicate, causing diseases by invading cells and disrupting their normal functions."},
    {"question": "What is Candidiasis?", "ground_truth": "Candidiasis is an infection caused by a species of the yeast Candida, usually Candida albicans. This is a common cause of vaginal infections in women."},
    {"question": "What is tetanus?", "ground_truth": "Tetanus is caused by Clostridium tetani, causing jaw stiffness followed by spasms (trismus), muscle stiffness, dysphagia, irritability, and hyperreflexia, with late painful convulsions."},
    {"question": "What is tuberculosis?", "ground_truth": "Tuberculosis is caused by Mycobacterium tuberculosis, with symptoms that are progressive and include cough, dyspnea, fever, night sweats, weight loss, and hemoptysis."},
    {"question": "What is anthrax?", "ground_truth": "Anthrax is caused by Bacillus anthracis, presenting with a persistent necrotic ulcer on exposed surfaces, regional adenopathy, and possible hemorrhagic mediastinitis from inhaled spores."},
