    {"question": "What is cryptococcosis?", "ground_truth": "Cryptococcosis is an opportunistic infection caused by Cryptococcus neoformans, most commonly causing meningitis in AIDS or immunocompromised patients."},
    {"question": "What is histoplasmosis?", "ground_truth": "Histoplasmosis is caused by Histoplasma capsulatum, often asymptomatic but causing cough, fever, malaise in self-limited infections, and disseminated disease in immunocompromised."},
    {"question": "What is coccidioidomycosis?", "ground_truth": "Coccidioidomycosis is caused by Coccidioides immitis from desert soil, causing fever, pleuritis, dry cough, erythema nodosum, and arthralgias, known as valley fever."},
    {"question": "What is pneumocystis pneumonia?", "ground_truth": "Pneumocystis pneumonia is caused by Pneumocystis jiroveci, seen primarily in immunocompromised patients with CD4 less than 200, causing fever, dyspnea, and diffuse alveolar infiltrates."},
    {"question": "What is sporotrichosis?", "ground_truth": "Sporotrichosis is caused by Sporothrix schenckii from plant or soil exposure, causing nodules along lymphatic drainage with possible ulceration and black eschar."},
