    {"question": "What is visceral leishmaniasis?", "ground_truth": "Visceral leishmaniasis (kala-azar) is caused by Leishmania donovani from sandfly bites, causing irregular fever with progressive skin darkening, cachexia, and marked splenomegaly."},
    {"question": "What is ascariasis?", "ground_truth": "Ascariasis is caused by Ascaris lumbricoides, with a pulmonary phase causing cough and eosinophilia, and an intestinal phase causing vague abdominal discomfort and possible obstruction."},
    {"question": "What is echinococcosis?", "ground_truth": "Echinococcosis (hydatid disease) is a zoonosis from dog tapeworm larvae, causing avascular cystic tumors of liver, lung, or brain with possible anaphylaxis on rupture."},
    {"question": "What is enterobiasis?", "ground_truth": "Enterobiasis is pinworm infection by Enterobius vermicularis, causing nocturnal perianal pruritus, insomnia, and restlessness, most commonly in children."},
    {"question": "What is schistosomiasis?", "ground_truth": "Schistosomiasis is caused by Schistosoma species, with acute Katayama fever and chronic sequelae including portal hypertension (S. mansoni) or hematuria (S. haematobium)."},

