    {"question": "What is gout?", "ground_truth": "Gout is a crystal-induced arthritis caused by deposition of monosodium urate crystals, classically causing nocturnal podagra (first MTP joint) pain, tophi, and hyperuricemia."},
    {"question": "What is pseudogout?", "ground_truth": "Pseudogout is calcium pyrophosphate dihydrate deposition disease causing subacute recurrent arthritis of large joints with chondrocalcinosis on x-ray."},
    {"question": "What is Behçet's syndrome?", "ground_truth": "Behçet's syndrome is a vasculitis usually in young adults from Mediterranean or Japanese ancestry, with recurrent painful oral and genital ulcers, uveitis, and skin lesions."},
