    {"question": "What characterizes Vitiligo?", "ground_truth": "Depigmented white patches surrounded by a normal, hyperpigmented, or occasionally inflamed border. Hairs in affected area usually turn white."},
    {"question": "What is acne vulgaris?", "ground_truth": "Acne vulgaris is a common disorder of the pilosebaceous unit with open and closed comedones, papules, pustules, and nodules, occurring at puberty and often persisting into adulthood."},
    {"question": "What is atopic dermatitis?", "ground_truth": "Atopic dermatitis is a chronic pruritic inflammatory skin disease, often starting in infancy, associated with a personal or family history of atopy, asthma, or allergic rhinitis."},
    {"question": "What is psoriasis?", "ground_truth": "Psoriasis is a chronic inflammatory skin disease with well-demarcated silvery-scaled plaques on extensor surfaces, associated with psoriatic arthritis in a subset of patients."},
    {"question": "What is seborrheic dermatitis?", "ground_truth": "Seborrheic dermatitis is a chronic inflammatory condition with greasy, scaly, yellowish patches on the scalp, face, and other sebaceous areas; in infants it is called cradle cap."},
    {"question": "What is basal cell carcinoma?", "ground_truth": "Basal cell carcinoma is the most common skin cancer, appearing as a pearly papule with telangiectasias or a rolled-border plaque, locally invasive but rarely metastatic."},
    {"question": "What is squamous cell carcinoma?", "ground_truth": "Squamous cell carcinoma is a skin cancer arising from sun-damaged skin, appearing as a hyperkeratotic, indurated papule or plaque that may ulcerate and metastasize."},
    {"question": "What is melanoma?", "ground_truth": "Melanoma is the most serious skin cancer, evaluated by ABCDE criteria: Asymmetry, Border irregularity, Color variation, Diameter over 6mm, and Evolving changes."},
    {"question": "What is actinic keratosis?", "ground_truth": "Actinic keratosis is a precancerous skin lesion from chronic sun exposure, appearing as discrete keratotic scaly papules on face, ears, scalp, and dorsal hands."},
    {"question": "What is scabies?", "ground_truth": "Scabies is a pruritic skin condition caused by the Sarcoptes scabiei mite, with intense nocturnal itching and burrows in finger webs, wrists, and genital areas."},
    {"question": "What is pediculosis?", "ground_truth": "Pediculosis is lice infestation; head lice cause scalp pruritus and nits on hair, body lice cause generalized pruritus, and pubic lice (crabs) are usually sexually transmitted."},
    {"question": "What is impetigo?", "ground_truth": "Impetigo is a superficial skin infection with rapidly spreading erythema, vesicles, or golden-crusted lesions, most commonly caused by streptococci or staphylococci."},
    {"question": "What is herpes zoster?", "ground_truth": "Herpes zoster (shingles) is a reactivation of varicella-zoster virus, causing painful vesicular rash in a dermatomal distribution, with possible postherpetic neuralgia."},

