    {"question": "What is acute cystitis?", "ground_truth": "Acute cystitis is infection of the bladder causing dysuria, frequency, urgency, hematuria, and suprapubic pain, usually caused by gram-negative bacteria such as E. coli."},
    {"question": "What is pyelonephritis?", "ground_truth": "Acute pyelonephritis is infection of the kidney and renal pelvis causing fever, flank pain, and vomiting, with pyuria, bacteriuria, and white cell casts in urine."},
    {"question": "What is nephrotic syndrome?", "ground_truth": "Nephrotic syndrome is characterized by proteinuria over 3 g/day, hypoalbuminemia, edema, and hyperlipidemia, with hypercoagulability and possible renal vein thrombosis."},
