    {"question": "What is acute kidney injury?", "ground_truth": "Acute kidney injury is an abrupt decline in kidney function, commonly caused by acute tubular necrosis, with oliguria, rising creatinine, and electrolyte abnormalities."},
    {"question": "What is chronic kidney disease?", "ground_truth": "Chronic kidney disease is progressive loss of kidney function over months to years, classified by GFR stages I-V, with complications including anemia, bone disease, and acidosis."},
    {"question": "What is benign prostatic hyperplasia?", "ground_truth": "BPH is nonmalignant enlargement of the prostate causing urinary hesitancy, weak stream, nocturia, and urgency, with possible urinary retention and azotemia."},
    {"question": "What is testicular torsion?", "ground_truth": "Testicular torsion is twisting of the spermatic cord causing sudden severe unilateral scrotal pain, with an asymmetric high-riding testis and absence of cremasteric reflex."},
    {"question": "What is kidney stones (urolithiasis)?", "ground_truth": "Urinary calculi are stones in the urinary tract causing sudden severe flank pain radiating to the groin, hematuria in 90%, nausea, and vomiting."},
    {"question": "What is bacterial prostatitis?", "ground_truth": "Bacterial prostatitis is infection of the prostate, with acute form causing fever, dysuria, perineal pain, and tender prostate, and chronic form causing recurrent urinary symptoms."},

