    {"question": "What is colic?", "ground_truth": "Colic is a syndrome of severe paroxysmal crying in infants, usually 1-3 months old, worsening in the late afternoon and evening, with a distended abdomen."},
    {"question": "What is enuresis?", "ground_truth": "Enuresis is involuntary urination at an age when control is expected (around age 5), mostly nocturnal, with 75% having at least one parent with similar history."},
    {"question": "What is ectopic pregnancy?", "ground_truth": "Ectopic pregnancy is implantation of the pregnancy outside the uterine cavity, most commonly in the fallopian tube, causing pelvic pain and bleeding and posing risk of rupture."},
    {"question": "What is pre-eclampsia?", "ground_truth": "Pre-eclampsia is hypertension and proteinuria after 20 weeks of gestation, with severe forms causing headaches, visual changes, and risk of seizures (eclampsia)."},
    {"question": "What is endometriosis?", "ground_truth": "Endometriosis is growth of endometrial tissue outside the uterus, causing cyclic pelvic pain, dysmenorrhea, dyspareunia, and infertility."},
    {"question": "What is acetaminophen poisoning?", "ground_truth": "Acetaminophen toxicity causes acute hepatic failure; N-acetylcysteine is nearly 100% protective if given within 8 hours of ingestion."},
    {"question": "What is carbon monoxide poisoning?", "ground_truth": "Carbon monoxide poisoning causes tissue hypoxia and affects organs with the highest oxygen demand (heart, brain), with nonspecific flulike symptoms, headache, and possible coma."},
    {"question": "What is organophosphate poisoning?", "ground_truth": "Organophosphate poisoning causes cholinergic excess (SLUDGE: salivation, lacrimation, urination, defecation, GI distress, emesis), with miosis, bradycardia, and bronchospasm."},
    {"question": "What is salicylate poisoning?", "ground_truth": "Salicylate poisoning causes mixed respiratory alkalosis and metabolic acidosis, with hyperpnea, tinnitus, confusion, and risk of seizures and pulmonary edema."},
